    {
      "bbox": [
        374,
        1667,
        1870,
        2083
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "A fundamental precept of sound management of any organization requires every employee and supervisor to understand the extent of his position, its responsibilities and its relationships to other positions and functions in the organization. In addition, in order to fulfill his responsibility as a member of management, every manager must know the lines of communication and control that operates within his administration, the relationships that exist between line and staff functions, and the need for inter-administration cooperation.",
